  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Five Card Stud Lowball. 2-10 players. 1 down, 1 up initially; 3rd-5th up. Four betting rounds. Highest upcard brings in (Ace low). Lowest hand showing acts first. Ace-to-five lowball: A-2-3-4-5 best. Straights/flushes ignored. Pairs are bad. Compare high cards first.',
    Player: "Welcome to Five Card Stud Lowball! This is Five Card Stud where the LOWEST hand wins. A-2-3-4-5 is the nuts. Highest card on board brings in, then lowest hand acts first. Avoid pairs at all costsâ€”they're terrible in lowball!",
    objective: 'Form the lowest possible 5-card hand. Lowest hand at showdown wins the pot.',
    gameplay: '1. **Ante**: All players post an ante. 2. **First Deal**: Each player receives 1 card face down and 1 card face up. 3. **Bring-in**: Player with the HIGHEST upcard (Ace counting as low) posts a compulsory bring-in bet. This is unique to lowballâ€”high card acts first and must bet. 4. **Subsequent Streets**: Three more cards dealt face up, with betting after each. 5. **Betting Order**: After the first round, betting begins with the player showing the LOWEST hand (pairs count as high). 6. **Showdown**: Best low hand wins.',
    keyRules: [
      'Lowest hand wins (ace-to-five ranking).',
      'Aces are always low (best card in the deck).',
      'Straights and flushes do NOT count against the player.',
      'A-2-3-4-5 (Wheel) is the best possible hand.',
      'First betting round: Highest upcard must bring-in (Ace is low, so King is worst).',
      'Subsequent rounds: Lowest hand showing acts first.',
      'Pairs are badâ€”you want five unpaired cards as low as possible.',
      'Compare highest cards first when breaking ties (7-5-4-3-2 beats 7-6-3-2-A because 5 < 6).',
    ],
